      "response": {
        "content": "I couldn't confirm that the order for REQ-1 went through, so I reported it as \"unknown\".\n\n- **Supplier choice:** S-1 quoted 5.40 USD per unit and S-2 quoted 5.75. Both are allowlisted and under the 6.00 limit. S-1 is cheapest, so the order was 100 units at a total of 54,000 minor units (540.00 USD).\n- **Approval:** Approval APR-0001 was granted for that order.\n- **Rejected submission:** My purchase order submission was rejected. The CC-OPS budget had changed since I read it, so the budget reading I cited was out of date. The rejection also said APR-0001 had already been used by an order, PO-0001.\n- **Evidence the order may exist:** The CC-OPS committed spend rose from 20,000 to 74,000. That is exactly 54,000 more, which fits a 100-unit order from S-1. I have no tool to look up PO-0001 and check.\n- **No resubmission:** I did not submit again, to avoid a duplicate order. The 26,000 left in the budget would not cover a second 54,000 order anyway.\n\nSomeone should check PO-0001 directly. The report lists no order ID, because the system only accepts one for a claim of \"done\".",
